invariant: INV-7
file: srv_quic.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the second ClientHello after a HelloRetryRequest asks
  choose_version again, so the server can change the negotiated version
  after it sent the retry in the first one, and the retry and the
  ServerHello go out in two versions. RFC 9369 section 4.1 has the server
  send every CRYPTO frame in the one negotiated version
  (rfc9369.txt:237-238). test/srv_quic_version_tests.h requires one call
  over ngtcp2's recorded retry round.

--- old
    rc = srv_check_retry_hello(h, &ch, &sel);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
--- new
    rc = srv_check_retry_hello(h, &ch, &sel);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
    rc = choose_version(q);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
